# Delete Account Sheet

::summary
The typed-confirm account deletion sheet (F-14), opened from Settings → About → Delete account (danger row): the cascade explanation, current password, then the typed confirmation — the delete button stays disabled until the exact phrase "delete my account" is typed. App Marketplace / Play subscriptions are NOT cancelled here.
::

::modal[name=delete-account title="Delete account" width=400 placement=centered dismissible=true]

:::callout[type=danger]
This permanently deletes your account, workspaces you solely own, docs, tasks, apps, messages, and files. App Marketplace / Play subscriptions are NOT cancelled here — manage those with the platform vendor or the store vendor.
:::

:::form[name=delete-account submit="Delete account" action=confirmDeleteAccount]
- Current password (password) *
- Confirmation (text, "Type delete my account to confirm") *
:::

::

Top-right ✕ per dismiss canon. The button enables only when the confirmation field exactly matches "delete my account" (case-insensitive, trimmed); confirming starts the deletion and signs out.

At small width (≤ 767px, R-C ruling 08-10) the sheet goes edge-to-edge with 10px side insets and auto width; the wide placement declared on the block is unchanged.
